# Configuration Guide

This project is for portfolio research: testing several strategies together as
one book.

```text
.env            research dates, image tag, and simulated portfolio capital
qkt.config.yaml data source and portfolio runtime settings
data/           local market data mounted into the QKT container
strategies/     portfolio and component strategy files
```

## .env

Edit the research window and simulated portfolio capital:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BACKTEST_FROM=2024-01-01
BACKTEST_TO=2024-02-01
QKT_STARTING_BALANCE=10000
```

`QKT_STARTING_BALANCE` is the allocation base for the portfolio research run.

## qkt.config.yaml

The generated config points QKT at local data and portfolio-oriented defaults.
Use it to keep the research setup reproducible instead of hiding assumptions in
one-off shell commands.

## Strategy Files

`strategies/portfolio.qkt` is the book. It references component strategies such
as `trend.qkt` and `mean_reversion.qkt`.

Run the book after edits:

```bash
make backtest
```

Before any live deployment, evaluate both individual strategy behavior and the
combined portfolio behavior.

